# The doc graph covers PROSE only — see docs/adr/0013.
#
# codegraph already owns code, and it owns it better: it returns a symbol's verbatim
# source in one call, which graphify structurally cannot (its nodes carry a start line
# and no text). codegraph in turn indexes neither shell nor markdown, which is most of
# what lives in THIS repo — hence the split. So this graph deliberately indexes no code
# at all, and the two never overlap. Everything here EXCLUDES; a .graphifyignore can only
# ever narrow, never re-include what .gitignore already dropped.
#
# Already excluded for free by .gitignore, so nothing below repeats them: the product repo
# clones (one anchored /<repo>/ line each, maintained by `aiworks add` / `aiworks remove`),
# node_modules/, agent_logs/, docs/brd/, mani.d/, the generated .cursor rule mirror, and
# the skill eval workspaces.

# ── everything that is not prose ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Excluding by TYPE rather than by directory is what keeps scripts/*/README.md and the
# other adapter docs in the graph while their shell and .env neighbours stay out. Those
# READMEs turn out to be the densest part of the graph, so a directory blacklist would
# cost more than it saves.
*.sh
*.py
*.js
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.ts
*.json
*.yaml
*.yml
*.toml
*.lock
*.html
*.css
*.txt
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.lua
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.pdf

# Extensionless shell scripts a type glob cannot catch.
/aiworks
/scripts/aiworks

# ── environment files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt and braces. .gitignore already drops .env and .env.*, and graphify honours it;
# restating the deny here means the boundary does not depend on one file. NOT negated for
# .env.example: a template holds no values, but it holds no prose worth a node either.
# .envrc is direnv's loader, which typically sources a real .env — it matches NEITHER
# `.env` nor `.env.*` (no dot after "env"), so nothing above catches it. graphify's own
# sensitive-file heuristic does flag it, but a heuristic in a pre-1.0 dependency is not a
# boundary worth relying on.
.env
.env.*
.envrc

# ── generated and archived duplicates ──────────────────────────────────────────
# .agents/ is the generated mirror of .claude/ (`aiworks cursor`). Indexing both would put
# two nodes on every skill and invent edges between a file and its own copy.
.agents/
.cursor/

# ── runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.superset/
.aiworks/
graphify-out/
.codegraph/
